/*  Getters and setters — a property read or written like a field. From `CheckGetterBody`,
    `CheckSetterBody`, `ValidateGetterSetterNames` and `FindSetterInOtOrPromoted` in
    `TypeChecker.Objects.cs`, and the getter and setter halves of `Pass1Hoist`.

    ★ In the tree: `(GetterDeclaration "name" <type> [body] <unto or _> line column)` and
    `(SetterDeclaration "name" <type> "parameter" [body] <unto or _> line column)`. One written
    inside its object is in the definition; one written `unto` a type is gathered into the checker's
    `untos` under `get <type>` or `set <type>`, beside that type's `unto` methods under its name.

    ⚠ A getter may not share a name with one of its object's stored fields; a setter may, and that
    is how a field gets a write hook.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Bind number to getter-row, given (the node getter):
        Return cast numeric on (cast field-of on (getter, 5)).
    Done.

    Bind number to setter-row, given (the node setter):
        Return cast numeric on (cast field-of on (setter, 6)).
    Done.

    /// Every getter an object has: its own, then those written `unto` it.
    Bind series of node to all-getters unto checker, given (the node definition):
        Define found as a series of node.
        For each getter in (cast field-of on (definition, 5))'s children, repeat:
            Insert getter into found.
        Done.
        Define attached as the entry for "get {cast def-name on (definition)}" in one's untos.
        If attached is not void:
            For each getter in attached's children, repeat:
                Insert getter into found.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    Bind series of node to all-setters unto checker, given (the node definition):
        Define found as a series of node.
        For each setter in (cast field-of on (definition, 6))'s children, repeat:
            Insert setter into found.
        Done.
        Define attached as the entry for "set {cast def-name on (definition)}" in one's untos.
        If attached is not void:
            For each setter in attached's children, repeat:
                Insert setter into found.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    /// The setter for a name — its own or an embedded object's — or void.
    Bind voidable node to setter-of unto checker, given (the text name, the text setter-name):
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
        If definition is void, return void.
        For each setter in cast one's all-setters on (definition), repeat:
            If cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (setter, 1)) is setter-name, return setter.
        Done.
        Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (definition).
        If embedded is "", return void.
        Return cast one's setter-of on (embedded, setter-name).
    Done.

    /// A write that a setter intercepts: the value must fit what the setter takes.
    Bind void or failure to check-setter-write unto checker, given (the node setter, the text member,
            the node value, the number at-row, the number target-depth, the text region-action):
        Define taken as cast field-of on (setter, 2).
        Define value-type as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (value-type) is false and cast assignable on (taken, value-type) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (value-type) or cast beyond-types on (taken):
                Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a {value-type's kind} through a setter")).
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("setter for '{member}' expects a {cast type-words on (taken)}, not a {cast type-words on (value-type)}", "",
                at-row, "set '{member}' to a {cast type-words on (value-type)}",
                "The setter for '{member}' accepts a {cast type-words on (taken)}.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's check-region-store on (value, value-type, target-depth, at-row, region-action) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// `ValidateGetterSetterNames`: no two getters or setters share a name, none shares a method's,
    /// and no getter shares one of the object's own stored fields.
    Bind void or failure to check-property-names unto checker, given (the node definition):
        Define name as cast def-name on (definition).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (definition, 9)).
        Define method-names as a map from text to fact.
        For each method in cast one's all-methods on (definition), repeat:
            In method-names, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1)) becomes true.
        Done.
        Define field-names as a map from text to fact.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (definition, 3))'s children, repeat:
            In field-names, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)) becomes true.
        Done.
        Define seen as a map from text to fact.
        For each getter in cast one's all-getters on (definition), repeat:
            Define getter-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (getter, 1)).
            If (the entry for getter-name in seen) is not void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' has two getters both named '{getter-name}'", "",
                    at-row, "define duplicate getter '{getter-name}'", "Each getter name must be unique. Rename one of them.")).
            Done.
            In seen, the entry for getter-name becomes true.
            If (the entry for getter-name in method-names) is not void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' getter '{getter-name}' clashes with a method of the same name", "",
                    at-row, "define getter '{getter-name}' when a method of the same name exists",
                    "Rename the getter or the method — getters and methods can't share a name.")).
            Done.
            If (the entry for getter-name in field-names) is not void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' getter '{getter-name}' has the same name as one of its stored fields",
                    "Every read of that name would reach the getter, so the field could be set but never read back",
                    at-row, "define getter '{getter-name}' beside a field of the same name", "Rename the getter or the field.")).
            Done.
        Done.
        Define seen-setters as a map from text to fact.
        For each setter in cast one's all-setters on (definition), repeat:
            Define setter-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (setter, 1)).
            If (the entry for setter-name in seen-setters) is not void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' has two setters both named '{setter-name}'", "",
                    at-row, "define duplicate setter '{setter-name}'", "Each setter name must be unique. Rename one of them.")).
            Done.
            In seen-setters, the entry for setter-name becomes true.
            If (the entry for setter-name in method-names) is not void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' setter '{setter-name}' clashes with a method of the same name", "",
                    at-row, "define setter '{setter-name}' when a method of the same name exists",
                    "Rename the setter or the method — setters and methods can't share a name.")).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A getter's body: no parameters, and every path gives back what it says it does.
    Bind void or failure to check-getter-body unto checker, given (the node getter, the text owner, the number self-row):
        Define getter-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (getter, 1)).
        Define returned as cast field-of on (getter, 2).
        Define body as cast field-of on (getter, 3).
        Define at-row as cast getter-row on (getter).
        Cast one's check-member-body on (owner, self-row, cast listed, at-row, false, returned, body) or pass the failure off.
        If cast definitely-returns on (body) is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "getter '{getter-name}' is declared to give back a {cast type-words on (returned)}, but it can reach its end without returning one", "",
                at-row, "define a getter that might not return a value",
                "Make sure every path through the getter ends with a return statement.")).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A setter's body: the incoming value is its one parameter, and it gives back nothing.
    Bind void or failure to check-setter-body unto checker, given (the node setter, the text owner, the number self-row):
        Define parameter as cast listed.
        Cast parameter's add on (cast field-of on (setter, 2)).
        Cast parameter's add on (cast field-of on (setter, 3)).
        Define parameters as cast listed.
        Cast parameters's add on (parameter).
        Cast one's check-member-body on (owner, self-row, parameters, cast setter-row on (setter), false, cast nothing,
            cast field-of on (setter, 4)) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// What a getter or setter written outside its object says this checker cannot judge yet, or "".
    Bind text to property-beyond-reach, given (the node declaration):
        Define typed as cast field-of on (declaration, 2).
        Define body as cast field-of on (declaration, 3).
        If declaration's kind is "SetterDeclaration", the body becomes cast field-of on (declaration, 4).
        If cast beyond-types on (typed), return "a {declaration's kind} of a {typed's kind}".
        Return cast beyond-reach on (body).
    Done.
Done.
